# the argument of republic-function.md by rule (phil/skeleton): connectives from the parse, an atom to each clause
logic	s5
atom	soul_end_else	and has not the soul an end which nothing else can fulfil ? for example to superintend and command and deliberate and the like
atom	function_proper_soul	are not these functions proper to the soul ?
atom	rightly_assign_other	can they rightly be assigned to any other
atom	other	to no other
atom	life_reckon_end	and is life to be reckoned among the ends of the soul ?
atom	assuredly_said	Assuredly he said
atom	soul_excellence	and has the soul an excellence also ?
atom	fulfil_own_end	and can she or can she fulfil her own ends when deprived of that excellence ?
atom	evil_ruler_superintendent(x)	x: then be an evil ruler and superintendent and the good soul a good ruler ?
atom	evil_soul(x)	x: evil soul
atom	admitt_justice_excellence	and we have admitted that justice is the excellence of the soul and injustice the defect of the soul ?
atom	admitt	that has been admitted
atom	live_well(x)	x: then will live well ?
atom	live_ill(x)	x: will live ill
atom	argument_prov	that is what your argument proves
atom	liv_well_bless	and he who lives well is blessed and happy ?
atom	liv_ill_reverse	he who lives ill the reverse of happy
atom	certainly	Certainly
atom	just_happy_unjust	then the just is happy and the unjust miserable ?
atom	happiness_misery_profitable	but happiness and not misery is profitable
atom	course	of course
atom	injustice_profitable_justice(x)	x: then injustice can be more profitable than justice
